,"answer":"A","topics":["money"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-12","type":"mc","prompt":"If a square's side-lengths are integers, its perimeter could be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"33"},{"key":"B","text":"44"},{"key":"C","text":"55"},{"key":"D","text":"66"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-13","type":"mc","prompt":"If 3 of every 150 astronauts walk on the moon, then \\underline{\\;?\\;}% of all astronauts walk on the moon.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"50"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-14","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the following, which *doesn't* reduce to $\\frac{3}{5}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{9}{15}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{21}{35}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{24}{40}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{33}{50}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-15","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\sqrt{100}=\\sqrt{36}+\\sqrt{\\underline{\\;?\\;}}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"64"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","algebra"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-16","type":"mc","prompt":"\\underline{\\;?\\;} can be made from 2 squares that share a common side.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"An octagon"},{"key":"B","text":"A hexagon"},{"key":"C","text":"A rectangle"},{"key":"D","text":"A triangle"}],"answer":"C","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-17","type":"mc","prompt":"By how much does the sum $19+28+37+46+55+64+73+82+91$ exceed the sum $18+27+36+45+54+63+72+81+90$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"9"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"90"},{"key":"D","text":"100"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic","patterns"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-18","type":"mc","prompt":"Uncle Bookworm eats two books a week; Aunt Bookworm eats one book every two months. In a year, Uncle eats \\underline{\\;?\\;} more books than Aunt.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"40"},{"key":"C","text":"80"},{"key":"D","text":"98"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","rates"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-19","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the largest odd factor of 81?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"27"},{"key":"D","text":"81"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-20","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^3=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{6}{9}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{8}{3}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{8}{27}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-21","type":"mc","prompt":"*At most* how many students can sit in a row of 25 chairs, if seated students must be separated by at least one empty chair?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"13"},{"key":"D","text":"24"}],"answer":"C","topics":["counting","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-22","type":"mc","prompt":"The smallest multiple of 10 that's greater than $9\\times9$ is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$9\\times9+10$"},{"key":"B","text":"$9.1\\times9.1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$9\\times10$"},{"key":"D","text":"$10\\times10$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-23","type":"mc","prompt":"The difference between $\\frac{5}{6}$ and its reciprocal is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{1}{5}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{1}{6}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{1}{30}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{11}{30}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-24","type":"mc","prompt":"On my scooter, the rear wheel's diameter is 6 cm more than the front wheel's. The rear wheel's circumference is \\underline{\\;?\\;} cm more than the front wheel's.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$3\\pi$"},{"key":"B","text":"$6\\pi$"},{"key":"C","text":"$9\\pi$"},{"key":"D","text":"$36\\pi$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-25","type":"mc","prompt":"A regular polygon is always","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"square"},{"key":"B","text":"equilateral"},{"key":"C","text":"scalene"},{"key":"D","text":"isosceles"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","logic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-26","type":"mc","prompt":"If I divide my age by 5, the remainder is 3. Your age is twice mine. If I divide your age by 5, the remainder will be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-27","type":"mc","prompt":"In a rectangle with perimeter 30 cm and area 56 cm$^2$, the longer side's length is \\underline{\\;?\\;} cm more than that of the shorter side.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"26"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-28","type":"mc","prompt":"If the sum of two whole numbers is 24 more than their difference, then one of the numbers *must* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"48"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-29","type":"mc","prompt":"The first 12 contestants won an average of \\$80. The next 20 won an average of \\$70. The 32 contestants won an average of","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"\\$73.75"},{"key":"B","text":"\\$74.75"},{"key":"C","text":"\\$75.00"},{"key":"D","text":"\\$75.75"}],"answer":"A","topics":["statistics","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-30","type":"mc","prompt":"$4^3\\times4^3=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$16^9$"},{"key":"B","text":"$16^6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$4^9$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4^6$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-31","type":"mc","prompt":"At most \\underline{\\;?\\;} circles of radius 1 with non-overlapping interiors can fit inside a square with side-length 4.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"16"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-32","type":"mc","prompt":"$0.1\\%=1\\%-\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.009%"},{"key":"B","text":"0.09%"},{"key":"C","text":"0.9%"},{"key":"D","text":"10%"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-33","type":"mc","prompt":"Today is my birthday. My age today, in months, is 72 times my age 5 years ago, in years. My age today, in years, is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"A","topics":["algebra","time-calendar"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-34","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\sqrt{\\sqrt{81\\times81\\times81\\times81}}=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"27"},{"key":"D","text":"81"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-35","type":"mc","prompt":"Of 2005 integers whose product is even, at most \\underline{\\;?\\;} can be odd.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2005"},{"key":"B","text":"2004"},{"key":"C","text":"1"},{"key":"D","text":"0"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","logic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":35},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-36","type":"mc","prompt":"The number \\underline{\\;?\\;} equals one-fourth of its own reciprocal.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac12$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac14$"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"A","topics":["algebra","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":36},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-37","type":"mc","prompt":"How many of the numbers $11, 21, 31, 41, 51, 61, 71, 81, 91$ are prime?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"6"},{"key":"D","text":"7"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":37},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-38","type":"mc","prompt":"$(301+302+303+\\ldots+325)-(1+2+3+\\ldots+25)=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"25"},{"key":"B","text":"2500"},{"key":"C","text":"5000"},{"key":"D","text":"7500"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","sequences-series"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":38},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-39","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the following, which is the first time after 4:30 that the minute and hour hands of my circular alarm clock *no longer* form an acute angle?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4:36"},{"key":"B","text":"4:37"},{"key":"C","text":"4:38"},{"key":"D","text":"4:39"}],"answer":"D","topics":["time-calendar","geometry"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":39},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g7-40","type":"mc","prompt":"Consecutive letters of the alphabet, starting with $A$, are given increasing consecutive integer values. If $H+K+L+N=2005$, then the average of all 26 of the consecutive integers is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"491"},{"key":"B","text":"498"},{"key":"C","text":"503.5"},{"key":"D","text":"505.5"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra","sequences-series"],"difficulty":3,"p":0,"n":40},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-01","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the following numbers, which is closest to 10.98?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10.00"},{"key":"B","t