,{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-08","type":"mc","prompt":"Three times a certain number is 36. One-third of that certain number is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"36"},{"key":"D","text":"108"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-09","type":"mc","prompt":"If a case of eggs contains 12 dozen eggs, how many eggs are in two crates of 12 cases each?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"48"},{"key":"B","text":"144"},{"key":"C","text":"288"},{"key":"D","text":"3456"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-10","type":"mc","prompt":"One hundred million divided by ten thousand equals","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"100"},{"key":"C","text":"1000"},{"key":"D","text":"10 000"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-11","type":"mc","prompt":"Ashley the chimney sweep puts his hat down on a square the same size as the opening of a chimney. The circular brim touches each side of the square at a single point. The perimeter of the square is 4 m. What is the radius of the circular brim of Ashley's hat?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.5 m"},{"key":"B","text":"1 m"},{"key":"C","text":"2 m"},{"key":"D","text":"4 m"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-12","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\frac13\\times\\frac24\\times\\frac35\\times\\frac46\\times\\frac57\\times\\frac68\\times\\frac79\\times\\frac{8}{10} = \\frac{1}{10}\\times\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{3}{19}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac29$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac19$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{2}{90}$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-13","type":"mc","prompt":"$20 + 30 + 40 - (\\text{the average of } 20, 30, \\text{ and } 40) =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"45"},{"key":"C","text":"60"},{"key":"D","text":"90"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","statistics"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-14","type":"mc","prompt":"Del loves sandwiches so much that 130 of his last 250 meals were sandwiches. What percent of those last 250 meals were *not* sandwiches?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"40%"},{"key":"B","text":"44%"},{"key":"C","text":"48%"},{"key":"D","text":"52%"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-15","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of the two least odd divisors of 120 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"15"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-16","type":"mc","prompt":"I collect 20 seashells every 30 minutes, but I drop 3 shells every 2 hours. If I collect shells for 8 hours, I will end up with $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ shells.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"68"},{"key":"B","text":"136"},{"key":"C","text":"296"},{"key":"D","text":"308"}],"answer":"D","topics":["rates","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-17","type":"mc","prompt":"The number of nickels in \\$3.00 plus the number of dimes in \\$6.00 is half the number of quarters in","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"\\$12.00"},{"key":"B","text":"\\$15.00"},{"key":"C","text":"\\$30.00"},{"key":"D","text":"\\$60.00"}],"answer":"D","topics":["money","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-18","type":"mc","prompt":"0.05% of 10 000 equals","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"50"},{"key":"C","text":"500"},{"key":"D","text":"5 000"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-19","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of 13 consecutive integers is 13. The greatest of the integers is","choi