t is open only on Monday through Friday each week, its 21st day open will be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"March 22"},{"key":"B","text":"March 23"},{"key":"C","text":"March 30"},{"key":"D","text":"March 31"}],"answer":"C","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-26","type":"mc","prompt":"Wilma's potion needs 3 ingredients. Her choices are newt, fly, beetle, snake, and snail. How many different combinations of 3 of these 5 choices are there?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"10"},{"key":"D","text":"60"}],"answer":"C","topics":["counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-27","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of six consecutive integers *could* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"81"},{"key":"B","text":"88"},{"key":"C","text":"92"},{"key":"D","text":"98"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-28","type":"mc","prompt":"288 minutes = $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$% of 1 day","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"15"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"40"}],"answer":"C","topics":["time-calendar","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-29","type":"mc","prompt":"Two cousins visited Jane today. One cousin visits every 42 days. The other visits every 429 days. They will next visit on the same day in $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ days.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4296"},{"key":"B","text":"6006"},{"key":"C","text":"9009"},{"key":"D","text":"18 018"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-30","type":"mc","prompt":"$3^{2013} - 3^{2012} =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$3^1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$3^{2011}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2\\times3^{2012}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$6^{1006}$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-31","type":"mc","prompt":"The measure of the smaller angle formed by the hour and minute hands of a circular clock at 2:46 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"84°"},{"key":"B","text":"137°"},{"key":"C","text":"167°"},{"key":"D","text":"174°"}],"answer":"C","topics":["geometry","time-calendar"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-32","type":"mc","prompt":"The median of $\\frac16, \\frac25, \\frac34, \\frac43, \\frac52$, and $\\frac61$ is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{669}{360}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{7}{12}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{25}{24}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["statistics","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-33","type":"mc","prompt":"Brad mixes seeds to attract birds. His Blue mix is 55% sunflower and 45% bluegrass. His Rye mix is 30% sunflower and 70% ryegrass. His Master mix combines some of each of the Blue and Rye mixes. If Master mix is 45% sunflower, how much of each kg of Master mix is Blue mix?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"350 g"},{"key":"B","text":"400 g"},{"key":"C","text":"600 g"},{"key":"D","text":"650 g"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-34","type":"mc","prompt":"If I multiply all whole numbers from 1 through 100, the largest power of 4 that is a factor of the product is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$4^{25}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4^{32}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$4^{48}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4^{50}$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g7-35","type":"mc","prompt":"Of my books, 85% are new and the rest are used. Some are biographies, 70% of which are new. What is the ratio of the fraction of new books that are biographies to the fraction of used books that are biographies?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"7:17"},{"key":"B","text":"14:17"},{"key":"C","text":"17:14"},{"key":"D","text":"17:7"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals","algebra"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":35},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-01","type":"mc","prompt":"$(2 \\times 4 \\times 8) \\div 2 = 4 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"16"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-02","type":"mc","prompt":"Al sleeps daily for 3 times as many hours as he is awake. For how many hours does Al sleep daily?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"18"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-03","type":"mc","prompt":"The number 36 is the product of $-6$ and","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$-6$"},{"key":"B","text":"$6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$-30$"},{"key":"D","text":"$42$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-04","type":"mc","prompt":"$20 \\times 18 = 20 \\times 19 + 20 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$-1$"},{"key":"B","text":"$0$"},{"key":"C","text":"$1$"},{"key":"D","text":"$20$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic","algebra"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-05","type":"mc","prompt":"Angel arrived $\\frac{3}{10}$ of an hour early for her noon appointment. At what time did Angel arrive?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11:18 a.m."},{"key":"B","text":"11:20 a.m."},{"key":"C","text":"11:40 a.m."},{"key":"D","text":"11:42 a.m."}],"answer":"D","topics":["time-calendar","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-06","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of the least and greatest positive odd factors of 2019 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"673"},{"key":"B","text":"2019"},{"key":"C","text":"2020"},{"key":"D","text":"6057"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-07","type":"mc","prompt":"The average value of the ten whole numbers from 0 through 9 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5.5"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"4.5"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"C","topics":["statistics","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-08","type":"mc","prompt":"$2019 \\times 3 + 2019 \\div 3 = 2019 \\times (3 +$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$$)$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac13$"},{"key":"C","text":"1"},{"key":"D","text":"3"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-09","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of four 4s equals the sum of $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ 4s.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"$3 \\times 4$"},{"key":"C","text":"$4^3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4^4$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-10","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the area of a square if one-third its side-length is 4?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"16"},{"key":"C","text":"48"},{"key":"D","text":"144"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-11","type":"mc","prompt":"On a Monday my surf club had 20 members. If the number of members doubled each day, on what day did my club first have over 2018 members?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Sunday"},{"key":"B","text":"Monday"},{"key":"C","text":"Tuesday"},{"key":"D","text":"Friday"}],"answer":"B","topics":["patterns","time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-12","type":"mc","prompt":"Rounding a decimal to the nearest whole number yields a number that is at most $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ greater than the original decimal.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.05"},{"key":"B","text":"0.1"},{"key":"C","text":"0.5"},{"key":"D","text":"0.9"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-13","type":"mc","prompt":"The perimeter of a rectangle with area 2019 and integral side-lengths is greatest when its length and width differ by","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"1"},{"key":"C","text":"670"},{"key":"D","text":"2018"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-14","type":"mc","prompt":"If half of my pals have at least 1 pet, and 1/3 of my pals with a pet have more than 1 pet, what fraction of my pals have exactly 1 pet?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac16$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac13$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac23$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac56$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-15","type":"mc","prompt":"The average of 0.5, 1.5, and 2.5 equals the average of 1 and","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"1.5"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"2.5"}],"answer":"C","topics":["statistics"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-16","type":"mc","prompt":"$9 \\times 90 \\times 900 \\times 9000 = 9 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$100^3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$900^3$"},{"key":"C","text":"$9000^3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$9\\,000\\,000^3$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-17","type":"mc","prompt":"What is one less than the product $-18 \\times 19$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$-341$"},{"key":"B","text":"$-342$"},{"key":"C","text":"$-343$"},{"key":"D","text":"$-344$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-18","type":"mc","prompt":"When I divide the number of digits in the decimal form of $10^{2018}$ by 4, the remainder is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"1"},{"key":"D","text":"0"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-19","type":"mc","prompt":"My first name has 60% as many letters as my last name. My first name *could* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Al"},{"key":"B","text":"Ali"},{"key":"C","text":"Alex"},{"key":"D","text":"Alexa"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-20","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the *least* possible sum of two integers whose product is 12?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$-13$"},{"key":"B","text":"$-11$"},{"key":"C","text":"$7$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-21","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the first 100 positive integers, $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ are *not* multiples of both 2 and 3.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"16"},{"key":"B","text":"32"},{"key":"C","text":"64"},{"key":"D","text":"84"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-22","type":"mc","prompt":"If one-third of the eggs in each carton of 1-dozen eggs are cracked, I must buy $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ cartons to get 16-dozen eggs that are *not* cracked.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"48"},{"key":"B","text":"36"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"20"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-23","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following is nearest in value to 8.25?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$8\\frac25$"},{"key":"B","text":"$8\\frac{2}{10}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$8\\frac{5}{10}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8\\frac{10}{25}$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-24","type":"mc","prompt":"I bowled on 2 days every week, on a different pair of days each week that I bowled. For at most how many weeks did I bowl?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"14"},{"key":"B","text":"21"},{"key":"C","text":"28"},{"key":"D","text":"35"}],"answer":"B","topics":["counting"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-25","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following has the least value?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.1"},{"key":"B","text":"0.01"},{"key":"C","text":"0.0011"},{"key":"D","text":"$(0.01)^2$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-26","type":"mc","prompt":"A rectangular prism is 5 m long, 4 m wide, and 6 m high. What is the sum of the lengths of its edges?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"15 m"},{"key":"B","text":"60 m"},{"key":"C","text":"80 m"},{"key":"D","text":"120 m"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-27","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the ratio of $1\\frac13$ to its reciprocal?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac34$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac43$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{16}{9}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-28","type":"mc","prompt":"Pens come in packs of 3, 6, 8, and 12. I bought 12 packs and got a total of 121 pens. If I bought at least one of each size pack, how many packs of 8 pens did I buy?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-29","type":"mc","prompt":"$3^2 \\times 8^2 \\times 5^2 = 6^2 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ $\\times\\, 10^2$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac12$"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"$2^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2^3$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-30","type":"mc","prompt":"I wrote the first 100 positive integers in order, and then erased every \"1\" I had written. How many digits did I erase?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"18"},{"key":"B","text":"19"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"21"}],"answer":"D","topics":["counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-31","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the difference between the product and the sum of the non-zero digits of $20^{10}$ when it is written in decimal form?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"$10^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2\\times10$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-32","type":"mc","prompt":"In the sequence $20, \\frac{19}{2}, \\frac{18}{3}, \\frac{17}{4}, \\ldots$, each term after the first term is gotten by subtracting 1 from the previous term's numerator and adding 1 to the previous term's denominator. How many terms in this sequence are positive integers?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"C","topics":["sequences-series","number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-33","type":"mc","prompt":"Two congruent rectangular cards partially overlap. The area of overlap is a square with area 4, and the total area of the regions of the faces of the two cards that do *not overlap* is 12. What is the area of one card?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"10"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-34","type":"mc","prompt":"If the mean of three positive integers is 5, then the product of all 3 integers is *at most*","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"105"},{"key":"B","text":"120"},{"key":"C","text":"125"},{"key":"D","text":"150"}],"answer":"C","topics":["inequalities","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g7-35","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the sum of the digits of the least 3-digit positive integer whose square is a 6-digit integer?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"9"},{"key":"D","text":"11"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":35}]}